{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Stateful.Rule</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"hegel","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Hegel","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Stateful","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Rule","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>One possible action in a sequential stateful test.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> <span>'state t</span></span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-create\"><a href=\"#val-create\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> create : \u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">name</span>:string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"optlabel\">?weight</span>:float <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">step</span>:<span>(<span><a href=\"../../index.html#type-test_case\">test_case</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span class=\"type-var\">'state</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"type-var\">'state</span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Declares a rule.</p><ul><li><code>name</code> is printed in the final output when the rule is run.</li><li><code>weight</code> is a hint of how frequently the rule should be run. The default weight is 1.0, and weights must be finite and strictly positive.</li><li><code>step tc state</code> performs one application of the rule, drawing any arguments it needs from <code>tc</code> and updating <code>state</code> in place. <code>tc</code> is valid only for that step.</li></ul><p>With the PPX, a rule takes the following option: <code>[@@rule { weight = ... }]</code>.</p><pre class=\"language-ocaml\"><code>let push =\u000A  Stateful.Rule.create\u000A    ~name:&quot;push&quot;\u000A    ~step:(fun tc stack -&gt;\u000A      let n = draw tc (integers ~min_value:0 ~max_value:100 ()) in\u000A      stack := n :: !stack)\u000A    ()\u000A;;</code></pre></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-name\"><a href=\"#val-name\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> name : <span><span><span class=\"type-var\">_</span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> string</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Returns the name of the rule.</p><pre class=\"language-ocaml\"><code>let label = Stateful.Rule.name push</code></pre></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-weight\"><a href=\"#val-weight\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> weight : <span><span><span class=\"type-var\">_</span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> float</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Returns the weight of the rule</p></div></div>"}